                                                "sense_id": "7a1d07e1-e4fe-38a9-8745-4e6941ecaf1d",
                                                "text": "In 1974, David Geffen, Asylum's main man, applied his negotiating abilities to creating a country-rock supergroup along the lines of Crosby, Stills & Nash."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57601633-7d66-424e-ba4a-ceb13e9d72b3",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1d07e1-e4fe-38a9-8745-4e6941ecaf1d",
                                                "text": "A supergroup is a rock and pop music term for a group whose members are already successful and well known, either as solo performers or part of other groups. It was first applied in 1968, to Cream, whose three members had already achieved prominence, […]"
